Jenkins Shared Libraries: DRY for Pipelines

In Jenkins, Shared Libraries let you store common pipeline code once and reuse it everywhere.
Think of them as your “central toolkit” for CI/CD.

What they do:
- Keep pipelines DRY (Don’t Repeat Yourself)
- Centralize shared functions, steps, and utilities
- Make updates easy: fix one place, apply everywhere
- Improve consistency and maintenance across teams

Shared Libraries turn Jenkins into a scalable, maintainable automation platform.
